From e801f50c80f273cb788e1fa58af0f2aadba57555 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neil Johnson <neil@soundsemiconductor.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:11:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] asxxsrc: an included file's .include and .incbin are
 found beside it

At the first line of an included file nxtline() did strcpy(afn,
asmc->afn) and set afp, leaving afs alone.  .include gives the new file
its includer's afn, so the copy was of a string onto itself - undefined
behaviour ASan reports as strcpy-param-overlap - and afs stayed the
includer's path while afp became the included file's path length.  The
.include and .incbin directives build a relative name from afs and afp,
so a file included from another directory could not include or take
anything beside itself:  sub/x.asm's .include "y.asm" opened the
includer's specification cut at the length of sub/'s path, with y.asm
after it.

The included file's afs and afp are now made current together, and afn
is left alone:  it is the source file's name, which symfn() prefixes to
the symbols it makes so that they are unique across modules.

astest, three new cases:  incpath fails before and passes after;  itst
(upstream's ascheck/itst, nested-include diagnostics) and incsym (the
symbols an included file makes are named after the module) were golded
with the unfixed assembler and pass unchanged.  52 of 52.  Sweep of
all 54 assemblers over the 171 sources under their own directories,
old and new builds:  2812 output files identical after the timestamps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 asxxsrc/aslex.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/asxxsrc/aslex.c b/asxxsrc/aslex.c
index 4e71ba5..2c46610 100644
--- a/asxxsrc/aslex.c
+++ b/asxxsrc/aslex.c
@@ -599,8 +599,8 @@ int skpcomma(void)
  *	side effects:
  *		include file will be closed at detection of end of file.
  *		the next sequential source file may be selected.
- *		The current file specification afn[] and the path
- *		length afp may be changed.
+ *		The current file specification afs, its name afn
+ *		and the path length afp may be changed.
  *		The respective line counter will be updated.
  *
  * --------------------------------------------------------------
@@ -898,7 +898,13 @@ loop:	if (asmc == NULL) return(0);
 			goto loop;
 		} else {
 			if (incline++ == 0) {
-				strcpy(afn, asmc->afn);
+				/*
+				 * The included file's own path, for the
+				 * .include and .incbin it contains.  afn
+				 * stays the source file's name:  the
+				 * symbols symfn() makes are per module.
+				 */
+				afs = asmc->afs;
 				afp = asmc->afp;
 			}
 			srcline = incline;
